## Requests::Request (Libraries/LibRequests/Request.h:46). (Filled by region p2d: the request of the
## RequestClient seam, DESIGN.md §7.1.) RefCounted and Weakable in C++; a cell here, so that
## FetchController holds it weakly (gc.Weak) and ResourceLoader roots it while it is active. The
## client delivers what it receives through requests_request_did_receive_headers, _did_receive_data
## and _did_finish, on the event loop; the data arrive as calls instead of through a pipe's
## descriptor (C++'s ReadStream and notifiers).
pub struct RequestsRequest: IsJsCell, gc.IsCell:
    pub var cell_base: JsCell  # primary base
    ## WeakPtr<RequestClient>: the client lives in the C heap for the process.
    pub var m_client: RequestsRequestClient*?
    pub var m_request_id: u64  # C++ default: { 0 }
    pub var m_mode: RequestsRequestMode  # C++ default: { Mode::Unknown }
    ## HeadersReceived on_headers_received.
    pub var on_headers_received: ak.Function3[HttpHeaderList*, u32?, ak.String?, unit]
    ## The DataReceived callback of set_unbuffered_request_callbacks (InternalStreamData's reader).
    pub var on_data_received: ak.Function1[const u8[], unit]
    ## RequestFinished on_finish.
    pub var on_finish: ak.Function3[u64, RequestsRequestTimingInfo, RequestsNetworkError?, unit]
    ## Function<CertificateAndKey()> on_certificate_requested.
    pub var on_certificate_requested: ak.Function0[RequestsRequestCertificateAndKey]
    ## The client's own state for the request (managed memory, kept by the cell's scan).
    pub var m_client_data: void*?

    func js_cell() -> JsCell*: return (JsCell*)&self

    func cell() -> gc.Cell*: return (gc.Cell*)&self

